{
	title: 'Web endpoint with a shared password',
	description: 'Smallest host side of a web client, for a trusted test deployment. Whichever process is host also listens on 127.0.0.1:web.port() (a config function, overridable from local.ts; default 9002) with Bun.serve, and stops with the host. GET / serves one page; POST /login with the right password (web.password(), default hello123, compared as plain text: this is a test, no crypto) sets a long-lived HttpOnly cookie holding that token, and a wrong one gets 401. A WebSocket at /ws requires the cookie and is one host.connect() connection: each message is one protocol command, each event goes out as one message, exactly like a socket client, so commands are validated the same way and several browsers and terminals can follow one session. Also serve the newest session id so a page can open the same conversation the terminal does, without the web code reading disk. Test with fetch and WebSocket against a temp home: login, bad password, no cookie, a submit streamed from a fake provider to both a web and an in-memory client.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['sj'],
	notes: [
		'Endpoint is src/host/web.ts; server.serve() starts it and server.stop() stops it. A busy port is logged to diag.log, not fatal.',
		'Page hook for dz: web.page() returns the GET / Response (placeholder now). Replace it, e.g. with a Bun.build bundle of src/web/.',
		'POST /login takes form data (field password) and answers 204 + Set-Cookie hal=<password>; HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Max-Age 10 years. Wrong password: 401.',
		'GET /session (cookie) returns the newest session id as plain text, 204 if none (sessions.newest(), moved from main.lastSession).',
		'/ws (cookie): each message is one ASON-encoded command; each event is sent as one ASON message (ason.stringify short). Parse with common ason.',
		'Tests set web.port = () => 0 (server.test, web.test, e2e local.ts) so they never touch the real 9002.'
	]
}
